{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Judah went down, etc.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory said (Sotah 13b) that his brothers brought him down from his greatness, and the Gaon Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra said that the reason is that one who comes from the north side of the world to its south is 'going down' — thus far. His words would be correct were it not that the verse says the phrase 'from his brothers,' which points with a finger that the descent was from his brothers. It further said <b>and he turned aside to a certain man, etc.</b>; and according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory the verse comes out precisely, for 'went down' (וַיֵּרֶד) intends the language of descent, and the phrase 'and he turned aside' (וַיֵּט) was needed for its own sake."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:50.721416062Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}